{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"agent_message","text":"Grouped GEMM is bit-exact, but ROCm’s current grouped implementation is slower than four graph-captured rocBLAS calls, so it is not a win. I’m using the final tuning window to test only the small output projections: if a Triton MFMA tile can match rocBLAS there, five output/stack launches can collapse to two; otherwise I’ll retain the verified 0.15 ms version."}}
